Z||000001||Bob Englert||01-19-2001||07:45 AM||||I think Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory in AL sells the FOCOA replacement EGR tube.  Call him at 256-420-5391 for more info.<P>You can also get a new GM factory repalcement tube from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A>  at a significant discount from the normal retail price.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||01-19-2001||12:28 PM||||Even better go grab one off of a 2.8L camaro/Firebird.  The holes on one of the flanges need to be elongated, but theyt fit perfectly. With three V6 cars around the house I always have at least one of these ready to go.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Predator||01-19-2001||12:58 PM||||I bought a new flexable one from Kevin at DesignoneSystems. It will never break since it is flexable. <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com</A> <BR>Get the number and call Kevin. The tube is not on the site, but if you goto contacts and call him, he can arrange to sell you one.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
